  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Premnath Tukaram More vs The Superintendent Of Police And ... on 13 June, 2024 Author: Shivkumar Dige Bench: Shivkumar Dige 2024:Bhc-Aug:10798 1 796.20 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay, Bench At Aurangabad. 919 Anticipatory Bail Application No. 796 Of 2024 Premnath Tukaram More ..Applicant -Versus- 1. State of Maharashtra 2. The Superintendent of Police ..Respondents ... Advocate for Applicant : Mr. P.P. More App for Respondent/State: Ms.R.P. Gaur ... Coram : Shivkumar Dige, J. Date : 13th June, 2024. P.C.: 1.",
    "facts": "The applicant apprehends arrest in connection with FIR No.115 of 2024 registered with Renapur Police Station, Tq. Renapur, Dist.Latur, for the offences punishable under sections 328, 188, 272, 273 of the Indian Penal Code (For short, \"IPC\") and under section 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act. 2. It is the prosecution case that one Vithal Londhe, Food Safety Officer, Latur has lodged the FIR stating that he has been appointed by the Commissioner of Food and Drugs Administration, Mumbai, to inspect food samples and to take action against prohibited food Premnath Tukaram More vs The Superintendent Of Police And ... on 13 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/196303963/ 1 articles. On 20th March, 2024, Mr. B. Chandrakant Reddy, Assistant Superintendent of Police informed that on 18 th March, 2024, he along with the police staff has conducted raid at Renapur in the shop of accused no.1 Bilal and accused no.2 Mehetabsab and seized 2 796.2024ABA.odt contraband articles from their shops. In the investigation, it revealed that the said Gutkha was purchased from the applicant and Firoz Umate.",
    "arguments": "3. It is contention of the learned counsel for the applicant that the applicant has been falsely implicated in this case. There is no recovery of Gutkha from the possession of the applicant. Mere on suspicion, name of the applicant is mentioned in the FIR. The learned counsel further submitted that the accused nos.1 and 2 have been released on anticipatory bail by this Court. Hence it is requested to allow the application. 4. It is contention of the learned APP that the police has seized the Gutkha from accused nos.1 and 2. The said Gutkha was purchased from the applicant and other accused. There is prima facie case against the applicant. Custodial interrogation of the applicant is required to inquire with source of Gutkha. Hence it is requested to reject the application.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. It is contention of the learned counsel for the applicant that the applicant has been falsely implicated in this case.",
    "respondent_arguments": "There is no recovery of Gutkha from the possession of the applicant. Mere on suspicion, name of the applicant is mentioned in the FIR. The learned counsel further submitted that the accused nos.1 and 2 have been released on anticipatory bail by this Court. Hence it is requested to allow the application. 4. It is contention of the learned APP that the police has seized the Gutkha from accused nos.1 and 2. The said Gutkha was purchased from the applicant and other accused. There is prima facie case against the applicant. Custodial interrogation of the applicant is required to inquire with source of Gutkha. Hence it is requested to reject the application.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
